### Post-Deploy Validation Skill - EOR Renewal Experiment Workflow

This skill validates recently launched Hivemind experiments by checking audience recording data flow and experiment health.

**Workflow scope:** Validation workflow only (workflow_intent = validate_experiment).

**CRITICAL: Single ticket only:**
- Validate ONLY the experiment from the Jira ticket provided by the user
- Do NOT search for other tickets with similar experiment names
- Do NOT infer or reference other tickets even if experiment names contain ticket IDs
- Do NOT attempt to find related experiments or prior versions
- Use only the Hivemind experiment URL from the provided ticket

**Do not use this skill for:**
- Ticket creation (use T1-T4)
- Opportunity sizing (use S1-S12)
- Experiment setup (use E1-E11)
- Gathering results (use R1-R8)

## Gate sequence

**IMPORTANT: V3 requires experiment_name from V4, so execution order is V1 → V2 → V4 → V3 → V5 → V6**

| Gate | Requirement |
|---|---|
| V1 | Jira ticket retrieved, Hivemind experiment ID and launch date extracted |
| V2 | Helix conversation session established |
| V4 | Hivemind experiment details retrieved via MCP (provides experiment_name) |
| V3 | Audience recording data validated using experiment_name from V4 |
| V5 | Count comparison complete (audience recording vs Hivemind) |
| V6 | Validation results posted as Jira comment |

**Gate order rationale:**
- V4 must execute before V3 because V3 needs the experiment_name from Hivemind
- V3 uses both experiment_name (from V4) and experiment_launch_date (from V1) in its query

